<!-- English translation of the upstream changelog (originally written in Chinese). -->

## [2.1.20261008222327] - 2026-10-08 22:23:27

### Debug

- Fixed the **error 1101** belief.

## [2.1.20260923155300] - 2026-09-23 15:53:00

### Debug

- Fixed the **local instance identifier**: unified how it is read from the header and the query key, so the identifier stays consistent across XHTTP padding, gRPC request detection and preferred-IP requests.
- Optimized **preferred-IP requests**: the local instance identifier is now appended to the User-Agent of requests to the preferred-IP API, the preferred subscription generator and the subscription converter, improving request correlation.

### Change

- Optimized **version detection**: the version query endpoint now always returns a numeric version.
- Optimized **subscription requests**: the current version number is now appended to the User-Agent of requests to the preferred-IP API, the preferred subscription generator and the subscription converter, so the server can identify the version.

## [2.1.20260922200117] - 2026-09-22 20:01:17

### Debug

- Fixed **aggregated subscriptions**: the User-Agent is now set consistently, making request behavior uniform.

## [2.1.20260907040834] - 2026-09-07 04:08:34

### ADD

- Added a **subscription converter setting**: the **expand full rule text** option.

## [2.1.20260904162413] - 2026-09-04 16:24:13

### ADD

- Added **ALPN** field support: node links now carry the ALPN parameter automatically, covering more client scenarios.

### Debug

- Fixed the **HTTPS proxy**: the handshake failed when the upstream server requested a client certificate (CertificateRequest); an empty certificate is now returned and the handshake completes normally. [Commit](https://github.com/cmliu/CF-Workers-CheckSocks5/commit/ae93bc28462a6df03795143a5caa85f717ba231a)

## [2.1.20260811144522] - 2026-08-11 14:45:22

### Change

- Optimized **XHTTP** upstream transport: added packet coalescing so small chunks are merged before sending, reducing frequent small writes, lowering resource usage and making large uploads smoother.

## [2.1.20260810030901] - 2026-08-10 03:09:01

### ADD

- Added receiver-side support for **XHTTP obfs padding**: recognizes the `xPaddingObfsMode` (tokenish / queryInHeader) obfuscation header.

## [2.1.20260809231057] - 2026-08-09 23:10:57

### Debug

- Fixed **XHTTP chained-proxy** parameter parsing: a trailing `/` on the path broke the reverse-proxy configuration; a trailing slash is now accepted.

## [2.1.20260809201158] - 2026-08-09 20:11:58

### Change

- Optimized the **XHTTP** transport path: TCP data now passes straight through in both directions via `request.body.pipeTo(socket.writable)` and `socket.readable.pipeTo(IdentityTransformStream)`, instead of going through ReadableStream + an upstream write queue + BYOB/Grain chunk-by-chunk copying, significantly reducing CPU usage.
- Optimized **XHTTP** connection management: `forwardataTCP` has a new "connect only" mode; once the connection is established and the first packet is written, the socket is returned directly for the pipe to take over. The fallback that switches to the reverse proxy automatically when a direct connection fails is kept (gRPC/WS callers are unaffected).
- Optimized **XHTTP UDP** handling: the UDP branch is split into a dedicated handler, keeping Trojan UDP reverse-proxy and DNS forwarding logic.

## [2.1.20260729235734] - 2026-07-29 23:57:34

### Change

- Corrected the **PRELOAD_RACE_DIAL** environment-variable logic: the default changed from `true` to `false` (preload race dialing is **off** by default); setting `1` or `true` turns it **on**. The README description of this variable was corrected as well. [Commit](https://github.com/IRNova/NovaWorker/commit/aea8b85688ef6066116af551cfd5e6fd2ce77567)

## [2.1.20260724150359] - 2026-07-24 15:03:59

### Change

- Synced the latest **GrainTCP** transport optimizations: the upstream Grain coalescing target changed from `16KB` to `20KB` and reuses a unified buffering/coalescing core; consecutive small chunks are merged opportunistically during drain, reducing high-frequency `writer.write()` calls. [Upstream commit](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Optimized downstream **GrainTCP** aggregation: the `32KB` aggregation cap is kept, using a `tail × 12` low-water mark and at most `4` growth probes of `1ms` each; flush can send several aggregated packets in a row and sends promptly near the cap, reducing the number of small WebSocket frames. [Upstream commit](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Optimized downstream packet handling: large chunks are sent directly when Grain is empty, small chunks first detach from the reusable read buffer on the BYOB/default reader path, and the aggregated result is copied before sending so reuse of the scratch buffer cannot overwrite data. [Upstream commit](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Enhanced TCP connection management based on the upstream transport model: added connection generation, socket identity and a drain barrier for the old downstream; during a redial, upstream data keeps being buffered and waits for the new writer, so asynchronous teardown of the old reader, timers or connection cannot contaminate the new connection. [Upstream approach](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Unified direct sends, segmented sends and timed flushes into one serial send chain based on the upstream Grain send model, and persisted asynchronous send errors; response headers are consumed only on the first real send, so a redial or a dead connection cannot consume the protocol response headers early. [Upstream approach](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Kept compatibility across the existing protocols: WS upstream uses non-blocking enqueue to reduce stalls in message handling, while XHTTP/gRPC keep waiting for the remote write to complete; the local upload high-water protection of `16MiB / 4096` entries is kept to prevent unbounded Worker queue growth. [Upstream change](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- The local speed-test response is now enabled only in **reverse-proxy mode**; when using **SOCKS5/HTTP/HTTPS/TURN/SSTP** proxies, speed-test requests are forwarded normally.

## [2.1.20260722191426] - 2026-07-22 19:14:26

### Change

- Adapted to the `http://cp.cloudflare.com/generate_204` real-connection test address.

## [2.1.20260711190235] - 2026-07-11 19:02:35

### ADD

- Added the **TCP_CONCURRENT_DIAL** environment variable to customize the **TCP concurrent dial count**; once set, dialing no longer drops to a single route on China Mobile networks automatically.
- Added the **PROXY_CONCURRENT_DIAL** environment variable to customize the **reverse-proxy concurrent dial count**.

## [2.1.20260711022318] - 2026-07-11 02:23:18

### Change

- Optimized **reverse-proxy logic**: fixed multiple reverse-proxy node parameters not taking effect because a global variable was overwritten unexpectedly.
- Optimized the **DoH cache**: recent domain resolution results are cached, cutting duplicate requests, speeding up resolution and lowering resource usage; domains that return no result are cached temporarily too, avoiding repeated lookups.

### ADD

- Added the **reverse-proxy concurrent dial count**: the number of concurrent reverse-proxy connections can be tuned. The higher the count, the faster the connection, but the more often the IP switches; the lower the count, the more stable the connection.
- Added **subscription converter options**: more feature options, including **UDP**, **XUDP**, **TLS 1.3**, **insert node type** and **basic node sorting**, passed through to the subscription converter backend.
- Added the **Trojan fallback proxy**: the Trojan protocol now supports a backup proxy address. When the primary connection fails, it switches to the backup proxy automatically and keeps working, making connections more stable and reliable. [PR #1359](https://github.com/IRNova/NovaWorker/pull/1359)

## [2.1.20260617014121] - 2026-06-17 01:41:21

### ADD

- The subscription converter options gained an **only output node info** option.

## [2.1.20260611041617] - 2026-06-11 04:16:17

### Change

- Optimized the UUID validation logic of the **version endpoint** to make validation more secure.

## [2.1.20260609132903] - 2026-06-09 13:29:03

### Debug

- Fixed the **error 1101** signature.

### Change

- Optimized the **PROXYIP resolution cache**: reverse-proxy addresses are lowercased before the cache comparison, so the same address is not resolved twice because of letter case.

## [2.1.20260601154939] - 2026-06-01 15:49:39

### Change

- Adapted to **Xray-core v26.2.6**: TLS removed the `allowInsecure` option, so the Base64 subscription no longer outputs **skip certificate verification**; Clash and Sing-box subscriptions are unaffected. [Release](https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core/releases/tag/v26.2.6)

## [2.1.20260529014818] - 2026-05-29 01:48:18

### Change

- Optimized direct access on **China Mobile**: TCP concurrent dialing drops to a single route, easing CPU timeouts.

## [2.1.20260526210857] - 2026-05-26 21:08:57

### Debug

- Fixed **TURN authentication**: an empty `REALM` in a STUN authentication challenge is now allowed, so an empty realm is not mistaken for a missing one and does not break the connection.

## [2.1.20260518183745] - 2026-05-18 18:37:45

### ADD

- Added the **PRELOAD_RACE_DIAL** environment variable to customize **TCP preload race dialing**: on the first direct connection to a domain, A/AAAA records can be queried concurrently over DoH, preferring IPv4 and topping up with IPv6 up to the `TCP concurrent dial count` limit; the reverse-proxy failure fallback is separated from a normal first direct connection, so preloading is not triggered by mistake.

## [2.1.20260517185203] - 2026-05-17 18:52:03

### Debug

- Fixed **WS/XHTTP/gRPC uploads**: upstream writes now wait for the remote write to complete before the next chunk is processed, so upload bursts no longer pile up inside the Worker and trigger `upload queue overflow`.
- Optimized the **explicit WS transport queue**: the upstream queue guard changed from 256KB to 16MB / 4096 entries, and waiting write tasks are released correctly when the queue is cleared, reducing occasional overflows during large uploads.

## [2.1.20260515185129] - 2026-05-15 18:51:29

### Change

- Optimized the **Shadowsocks subscription**: when TLS is off, the preferred port is rewritten to the noTLS port automatically. (This does not apply to reverse-proxy IPs.)
- Optimized the **GO2SOCKS5** variable: changed from override mode to append mode. [PR #1202](https://github.com/IRNova/NovaWorker/pull/1202)

## [2.1.20260513042803] - 2026-05-13 04:28:03

### Change

- Optimized the **VLESS** hot path: the UUID is pre-decoded to 16 bytes for direct comparison, and first-packet parsing now uses offsets and `subarray()` with fewer copies. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP)
- Optimized **WS Early Data**: added an 8KB upper-bound guard and prevented ordinary WebSocket subprotocols from being mistaken for early data and injected into the first packet. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP)
- Optimized the **WS/XHTTP/gRPC** upstream path: added a bounded queue, small-packet coalescing and 256KB backpressure protection, cutting high-frequency small writes and preventing unbounded queue growth. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP)
- Optimized the downstream **GrainTCP** send path: small packets are aggregated with a microtask and a short quiet window, while large packets flush the aggregator first on the BYOB path and are then sent directly, reducing copies and the number of WebSocket frames. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP)
- Optimized the TCP connect flow: direct and proxyip reverse-proxy candidates now use 4 concurrent dials racing for the first successful connection, while SOCKS/HTTP/HTTPS/TURN/SSTP proxy chains keep their original handshake logic. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP)
- Optimized the WebSocket handshake and the WS main transport: `allowHalfOpen` gained an exception fallback, the 101 response clears `Sec-WebSocket-Extensions`, and the WS main path now uses an explicit ordered queue. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP)

## [2.1.20260511041705] - 2026-05-11 04:17:05

### Change

- Optimized the password validation on the **login settings page**: a stray newline when a beginner sets the `ADMIN` password no longer makes the password impossible to enter and drives them up the wall!

### Delete

- Removed the request-count refresh countdown from the subscription response headers, so beginners do not see it and lose their temper!

## [2.1.20260508190728] - 2026-05-08 19:07:28

### Debug

- Fixed **random preferred IP** generation: carrier information was lost after subscription conversion, so preferred IPs for the matching carrier could not be generated.

### Change

- Optimized subscription conversion: a temporary `TOKEN` is submitted for the conversion, so the real subscription URL is not leaked.

## [2.1.20260508041513] - 2026-05-08 04:15:13

### Change

- Optimized the **PROXYIP** domain resolution flow: for a domain, the reverse-proxy address is read from the **TXT** record first, and the **A** record result is used when TXT returns nothing.
- When both TXT and A records return nothing, the **AAAA** record is queried, reducing unnecessary IPv6 lookups.

### Delete

- Removed the `.william` domain special case and the Google DoH fallback retry logic; ordinary domains can now configure a reverse-proxy address through TXT records as well.

## [2.1.20260506175102] - 2026-05-06 17:51:02

### New

- Added **TURN protocol** proxy support to reverse-proxy mode. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/CF-Workers-TURN)
- Added **SSTP (SoftEther) protocol** proxy support to reverse-proxy mode. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/CF-Workers-SoftEther)
- Added the ability to create **chained proxy** nodes in custom subscriptions.

## [2.1.20260503011925] - 2026-05-03 01:19:25

### Change

- Adapted **Sing-box** support for the ECH custom **EchConfig resolution domain** feature.
- **Custom subscriptions** now support wildcard preferred domains.

### Delete

- Removed the **EchConfig DNS service** backup DoH for ECH in **Clash**.

## [2.1.20260417015756] - 2026-04-17 01:57:56

### Debug

- Synced upstream project updates and fixed known **HTTPS proxy** issues. [Reference link](https://t.me/Enkelte_notif/824)
- Fixed known issues [#1117](https://github.com/IRNova/NovaWorker/issues/1117) [#1119](https://github.com/IRNova/NovaWorker/issues/1119) [#1120](https://github.com/IRNova/NovaWorker/issues/1120)

## [2.1.20260416044724] - 2026-04-16 04:47:24

### New

- The Trojan protocol now supports DNS queries over UDP Over TCP.
- Added **HTTPS proxy** support to reverse-proxy mode. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/CF-Workers-HTTPS)

## [2.1.20260413174651] - 2026-04-13 17:46:51

### Change

- Optimized the WebSocket data-transfer logic and added BYOB mode support for better performance and flexibility.

## [2.1.20260410060317] - 2026-04-10 06:03:17

### New

- Added **AEAD encryption** to the Shadowsocks protocol, providing content encryption for non-TLS transports.

## [2.1.0]

### New
- The VLESS/Trojan protocols now support XHTTP and gRPC transports.

## [2.0.0]

### New

- The project architecture was fully rewritten and a front-end web page was added. [Front-end source](https://github.com/Nova-Panel/nova-panel.github.io)
